# module MSBuild vendored NuGet integration

Detect the lexicographically first root `.csproj` or `.fsproj` and consume a `nuget` export only
when the dependency has a locked vendor. The export path names either the vendored project file
or its containing directory; a directory must contain exactly one root project file. The exact
project-file form is available during mutation preflight before the vendor tree is materialised
and is therefore the recommended public contract.

# decision One generated targets file and one marked project import

`deps/git-a2a.targets` contains sorted `ProjectReference` blocks and is wholly owned by git-a2a.
The consumer project receives exactly `<Import Project="deps/git-a2a.targets" Label="git-a2a" />`
before its closing `Project` element. Wire discards foreign generated bytes with a warning, Drift
reports them, and Unwire always repairs or removes the generated file without touching other XML.
Each block removes the vendored project's C# and F# sources from the consumer SDK's recursive
default `Compile` glob before adding `ProjectReference`, preventing duplicate compilation.

# test Golden and real-toolchain lifecycle

Fixture tests cover C# and F# detection, idempotence, drift, foreign-content repair, sorted blocks,
and byte-restoring Unwire. The opt-in integration job runs a real `dotnet build` against a copied
vendored C# project.
